 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Roll the anko into <b>6 balls of <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"35\" data-s=\"0\">35 g</span></b> and set them on a plate in the fridge.</li><li>If it's too soft to hold a shape, stir it in a pan over low heat for a few minutes to dry it out, then cool it. Firm anko is much easier to wrap.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll the anko",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Roll each ball between your palms; firm anko wraps more easily.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/1-how1.webp?v=2702567791"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/1.webp?v=4846b18b56",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Roll the anko",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"210\">210 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Anko (red bean paste)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>In a heatproof glass bowl, stir the <b>shiratamako</b> and <b>sugar</b> together.</li><li>Add the <b>water</b> a little at a time, stirring and pressing out the lumps, until it's smooth and pours like thick cream.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix the batter",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Add the water a little at a time and press out the lumps.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/2-how1.webp?v=f3803e86ca"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/2.webp?v=54e1a4e807",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>3 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix the batter",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\">100 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Shiratamako (glutinous rice flour)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"30\">30 g</span>",
     "name_html": "White sugar"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"120\">120 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cover loosely with cling film. Microwave <b>1 minute</b> at 600–700 W, then stir hard with a wet spatula. The edges will have set first.</li><li>Another <b>1 minute</b>, stir again. It's now a sticky lump.</li><li>Another <b>20–30 seconds</b>, until the whole mass is <b>translucent</b>, glossy and stretchy, with no opaque white patches. Stir once more.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Microwave in three bursts",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "1 minute, then stir hard with a wet spatula: the edges set first.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/3-how1.webp?v=a7e3246f99"
     },
     {
      "caption": "After the last burst it's translucent and stretchy all through.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/3-how2.webp?v=c418a929c3"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/3.webp?v=6809e64653",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Microwave in three bursts",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Sift a thick layer of <b>potato starch</b> over a tray. Scrape the hot mochi onto it and dust the top too.</li><li>With a dusted bench scraper, cut it into <b>6 even pieces</b>, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"40\" data-s=\"0\">40 g</span> each. Wait a minute or two, until you can handle it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Divide on starch",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cut into six with a dusted bench scraper.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/4-how1.webp?v=5d6bb65e61"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/4.webp?v=0541aebcb2",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Divide on starch",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\">3 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Potato starch (katakuriko)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take one piece and stretch it into a disc about <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"8\" data-s=\"0\">8 cm</span></b> across with starchy fingers. Make the edge a little thinner than the middle.</li><li>Set an anko ball in the middle.</li><li>Pull the edge up over the ball in four or five pleats and <b>pinch them together</b> on top. Twist off any extra.</li><li>Turn it over so the seam is underneath, and cup it in your palm to round it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap and pinch shut",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stretch a piece into an 8 cm disc, edge thinner than the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/5-how1.webp?v=3a8d64a276"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Anko ball in the middle; pleat the edge up over it and pinch shut.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/5-how2.webp?v=20a6d0d7f7"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/5.webp?v=a53ef04ee7",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>10 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap and pinch shut",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Brush off the loose starch.</li><li>Serve the same day, at room temperature. Cut one in half with a wet knife to show the thick dark anko in its thin white shell.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Brush and serve",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Brush off the loose starch; cut with a wet knife to show the inside.",
      "src": "illustrations/daifuku/6-how1.webp?v=4c7b5e452f"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/daifuku/6.webp?v=6ac7d6941b",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>2 min</span>",
   "title": "Brush and serve",
   "uses_rows": []
  }
 ],
